  body: "## Intent\n\ngsp-80r2c: on a Pipe deal record, make every contact's email in the contacts list a mailto: link (done and repo on the bead: br show gsp-80r2c --db ~/dev/gsp-beads/.beads/beads.db).\nThe bead, from a reporter's in-app report on /deals/10000097: on a deal record, the email shown for a contact should be a clickable mailto link so the reporter can click it and have their mail client open addressed to that person. The reporter was looking at the contacts area of the deal (the list under \"Add a contact\") and saw the contact's email as plain text rather than a link.\n\nSo, the email is now a link, that works - but it does not fill in the subject line like I asked.\n\nDone: on a Pipe deal page, clicking a contact's email (the contacts list and the primary contact line) opens a new message to that person with the deal's name as the subject, URL-encoded (deal 10000097 'Caterpillar VR' opens subject 'Caterpillar VR'). Checked live in production on deal 10000097, then Dan gets the one it's-live note on this report (scripts/reporter-ready.ts gsp-80r2c --vouch). Left alone: email links on the contacts, contact and org pages (no deal there). The Correspondence 'Reply all' link (gsp-cteur) already fills 'Re: <subject>' and stays as it is.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Add the URL-encoded deal name as the subject in contact-list and primary-contact `mailto:` links.\n- Extend rendering and interaction tests to cover encoded subjects and deal-page propagation.\n- Update Pipe’s email-link documentation and the primary-contact anchor’s ESLint contract fingerprint.\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n✅ Low: Both intended email paths use the URL-encoded saved deal title, while unrelated links and access controls remain unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n\nThe four focused regression files and isolated real-product browser scenarios passed. Screenshots and decoded mail handoffs were retained using a registered local capture composer. Browser setup failures were corrected, disposable resourc