      body: "carmanchip23-dev: APPROVE.\n\nWhat I Verified\n\n- I reviewed all 7 changed files at 85c059c00d957a6b39485bcb2e5e06175bc8784c. Both deal-page mailto surfaces now derive the subject from the saved deal title and encode it with encodeURIComponent; the contact-list path deliberately uses initial.title, so an unsaved edit cannot leak into the subject, while the primary-contact path receives the same persisted deal.title from the server-rendered page.\n- The regression coverage exercises both links, keyboard activation, propagation through DealPage, two contacts, and reserved/Unicode characters (`Acme & Café #1`). I also checked that the no-email behavior remains non-link text and that unrelated Correspondence behavior is untouched by the implementation.\n- The near-code README now describes the same behavior, and the required Pipe/packages/suite/docs and repository checks are green on this head. There are no standing reviews or comments to override.\n\nThe strongest thing I could not independently check is the handoff into each user's external desktop mail client or the deferred production acceptance on deal 10000097; I checked the generated mailto contract and its automated/local-browser evidence, not those external environments. That does not undercut the implementation claim on this head.\n"
