  body: "## Intent\n\nBead gsp-cteur was reopened on Dan's ask (PM inbox 1792158058-2ZLyDX): make each Correspondence message's Reply all a small outline button like Refile (Button asChild around the existing mailto link, same href and data-slot). Done and the file are on the bead's newest EP comment. Bead gsp-cteur holds the done: read it with `br --db ~/dev/gsp-beads/.beads/beads.db show gsp-cteur` and its comments; that Done is the acceptance criterion.\n\nDone: on a Pipe deal page, each Correspondence message's Reply all reads as a small outline button like Refile (Button variant outline, size sm, as a link-button: Button asChild around the existing link), with the same mailto (To, Cc, 'Re: <subject>'), the same data-slot reply-all, a visible focus ring and keyboard reach. Checked live in production on deal 10000097, then Dan gets the one it's-live note on this report (scripts/reporter-ready.ts gsp-cteur --vouch). Code: apps/pipe/src/app/deals/[id]/Correspondence.tsx (Reply all is a bare NavLink today).\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Render each Correspondence message’s Reply all link as a small outline `Button` using `asChild`, matching Refile.\n- Preserve the existing mailto URL and `reply-all` data slot, and align the button with `self-start`.\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n✅ Low: The requested Button wrapper preserves mailto generation, the reply-all slot, access boundaries, and native keyboard behavior across message paths.\n\n## Testing\n\nTargeted correspondence/mailto tests and live checks of the isolated authenticated Pipe deal passed; before/after screenshots and rendered measurements confirmed matching outline buttons, unchanged hrefs, and keyboard focus. Setup mismatches were corrected, the target was restored exactly, and disposable resources were removed. Production confirmation and Dan’s note remain post-deployment.\n\n- Live validation: ✅ go - 3 of 5 scenarios driven live against the product\n\n| Scenario | Result | Live | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- 