      body: "carmanchip23-dev approves this change.\n\n## What I Verified\n\n- The entire PR is one file and `+6/-3`: it replaces the bare per-message `NavLink` with the shared `Button` using `variant=\"outline\"`, `size=\"sm\"`, and `asChild`, while leaving `replyAllHref` construction and `data-slot=\"reply-all\"` unchanged.\n- I read the shared `Button` and `NavLink` implementations. Radix `Slot` merges the button styling onto the link, so the result remains one anchor rather than nested interactive elements; `NavLink` treats `mailto:` as external and deliberately leaves non-HTTP protocols to native navigation.\n- The `self-start` class prevents the control from stretching across the message column. Its shared outline/small variants are the same variants used by the adjacent Refile control.\n- The SHA-bound record covers three rendered Reply all anchors: all remained keyboard reachable with visible focus, all measured 32px high with a 1px outline matching Refile, and all retained distinct mailto recipients/subjects. Pipe, suite, required verification, docs integrity, and migration checks are green on `60f1084afa62559cf4c8ea89df23955e4ac3df53`.\n\nI did not independently rerun the authenticated browser screenshots or launch an operating-system mail client. I reviewed the recorded browser measurements and activation evidence as a record, including the negative-control baseline; the code path itself preserves the existing href and native mailto behavior.\n"
